uploads/

# Misc
# The blanket image rules exist to keep dataset frames and scratch screenshots
# out of the repo. They are NOT meant to catch authored UI assets, and they were
# silently excluding two sets that the app cannot run without.
*.jpg
*.png
*.jpeg

# Authored UI assets — required at runtime, so they must be tracked.
# manifest.json declares the three icon sizes by name; without them Chrome
# refuses to load the unpacked extension. The brand logo is referenced by five
# components via /brand/, so an untracked copy means a clean clone builds
# successfully and then renders broken images.
!extension/assets/*.png
!safe-test-dashboard/public/brand/*.png

# Packed extension. Regenerated from extension/ on demand and ~22 MB a copy, so
# every re-pack would add another full blob to history for a file that is a pure
# function of tracked sources. The models under backend/static/models/ are the
# opposite case and ARE tracked: they are build OUTPUTS of the training scripts,
# but nothing in the repo can reproduce them without the dataset and a GPU.
ai-observer-extension-v2.0.0.zip
*.crx

# Scratch backups taken while re-exporting the classifier at 224 (best.pt.demo,
# best.onnx.224demo, served_best.onnx.224demo). Superseded by the tracked
# weights/best.onnx, and ~15 MB. Safe to delete.
_demo_backup/

# Local Claude Code configuration. settings.local.json is machine-specific by
# name and already ignored by the tool's own convention; claude.md here is empty
# and the authored guidance lives in the tracked CLAUDE.md at the repo root.
.claude/
